{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/780","id":5202761364,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTty1_c8AAAABNhvWlA","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/780","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/780.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/780.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/issues/780","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/780/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/780/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/issues/780/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/statuses/68c664332e340591e629c4db0f611f11e33135f1","number":780,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(pon): reserve ACK signatures before native dispatch","user":{"login":"ProfHepta","id":102159240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhbTiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102159240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta","html_url":"https://github.com/ProfHepta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\n\nUnauthenticated caller and operation claims must not spend another account's authorization. Native work can also complete while a later authentication burst prevents its ACK signature. Both are local admission and accounting failures; rejected W1 transcripts do not establish forged valid blocks.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Integrate the reviewed r16 ingress boundary and r17 response reservation with the existing throughput candidate, preserving its bounded decoder, socket reads, source guards and retained failure evidence.\n- Reserve response signing principal and a slot from the original authentication budget after authenticated dequeue and before native dispatch. The unique reservation is consumed without a second capacity race.\n- Retain pending/running CPU reservations until actual worker settlement. Preserve native commit facts when response encoding, signing, cancellation or transport fails.\n- Include classical and PQ pending/unknown obligations in final listener, History and continuous-owner settlement. PQ retains its original finite lifetime limits and gains a stricter two-slot sublimit.\n- Add real TCP and owner-boundary controls, including a required TCP EOF observation in the cancellation test. Update current policy namespaces and exact current-source pins; retain historical vectors and receipts.\n\n## Validation at publication\n\nCandidate: 33fdb7a2721ee8e4ff42a7ab0a7b57a90ba254d2.\nComplete tracked source verified: 11,018 entries / 1,032,289,893 bytes.\nPinned formatting, distributed source inventory, all 26 workflow literal source guards and the 573-blob PQ source guard pass. The PQ guard remains HOLD_NO_GO and grants no cryptographic acceptance.\nThe exact OpenSSL 3.5.9 source was freshly built and passed ML-DSA-65 sign/verify/wrong-message smoke. Earlier download failures are retained separately.\nThe pre-integration r17 checkpoint passed 4 classical and 6 PQ reservation unit controls. Those are not claimed as final combined-source or TCP qualification.\nFinal combined-source native component tests, strict Clippy, negative source controls, Cargo graph checks and original hosted qualification are pending/running.\n\n## Unchanged acceptance and limits\n\nKeep the original public Host at 0.25 CPU, 2 GiB, zero swap, 256 PIDs, and the original 4-second / 16-hostile gate. Keep three complete 0/24/24 campaigns, full 4,105-block History, capacity/churn and independent WAN acceptance as separate requirements. Desktop component runs cannot substitute for those gates.\nThe prospective-merge lane for this PR binds the actual integration base, not main.\nA reservation does not guarantee delivery after deadline, cancellation, provider/accounting failure, network loss or an actual PQ lifetime overrun. Pending response slots can also delay later requests; honest completion and tail latency still require the original load acceptance.\nNo anonymous fairness, valid-work cost lower bound, single-node economics, production activation, force push or main merge is claimed.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-07T14:52:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T15:22:34Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:fix/chain-w1-ingress-integrated-20261107","ref":"fix/chain-w1-ingress-integrated-20261107","repo":{"id":1323087357,"node_id":"R_kgDOTty1_Q","name":"Trillionnium-Chain","full_name":"TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain","owner":{"login":"TrillionniumFoundation","id":262513357,"node_id":"O_kgDOD6WizQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262513357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation","followers_ur